Version 1.34.0 — 2026-11-16
Previous GitHub release: v1.33.0 (2026-11-16)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.34.0 adds a ".prj file check": it verifies that the projection
file exists, can be read and matches the CRS of the layer.

Changes in 1.34.0
-----------------
- Added the ".prj file check" for Shapefile datasets:
  - a missing .prj (or .qpj) file is flagged;
  - an unreadable, empty or non-WKT .prj is flagged;
  - unbalanced brackets or an unknown WKT root are treated as broken
    WKT;
  - the CRS type (geographic or projected) from the .prj is compared
    with the CRS of the layer;
  - the EPSG code from the .prj, when present, is compared with the
    layer CRS.
- The check is optional and disabled by default.
- The "Metadata and CRS" check no longer reports a missing .prj when
  the new check is selected, so the same problem is reported once.
- Russian and English interface strings, README, metadata and tests
  were updated.

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.34.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

