Version 1.33.0 — 2026-11-16
Previous GitHub release: v1.32.0 (2026-11-16)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.33.0 adds a separate "Geometry validity check" and a separate
coordinate check: NaN/Inf, excessively large values, swapped latitude
and longitude, coordinates outside the valid CRS range.

Changes in 1.33.0
-----------------
- The former "Geometry and coordinate check" is split into two checks:
  - "Geometry validity check" — self-intersections, unclosed rings,
    empty and null geometries;
  - "Coordinate check" — NaN/Inf, excessively large values, swapped
    latitude and longitude and coordinates outside the valid CRS range.
- Both checks are optional, disabled by default and have their own
  description panel with actions and examples.
- Check statistics, Excel and HTML reports show the two checks as
  separate sections and rows.
- Russian and English interface strings, README, metadata and tests
  were updated.

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.33.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

