Version 1.29.0 — 2026-11-15
Previous GitHub release: v1.27.0 (2026-11-13)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.29.0 adds a "Copy to …" button for selected files. It copies
complete datasets, including sidecar files, to a chosen folder.

Changes in 1.29.0
-----------------
- Added the "Copy to …" button at the bottom of the "Files" tab.
- The button is enabled when one or more files are selected.
- Selected datasets are copied together with their sidecar files:
  Shapefile, MIF/MID, MapInfo TAB, CSV and raster sidecars are included.
- Copying runs with a progress dialog showing the current file and size;
  the operation can be cancelled.
- Files are written through a temporary file in the destination folder
  and replace the target only after a successful copy, so cancellation
  or an error does not corrupt an existing destination file.
- Existing files with the same names require explicit overwrite
  confirmation.
- Duplicate names between different selected datasets stop the copy
  with a clear message instead of silently overwriting data.
- Copying into the source folder itself is skipped safely.
- The destination folder is remembered and used as the starting folder
  next time.
- Copy errors are reported per file; successfully copied files remain.
- Russian and English interface strings, README, metadata and tests
  were updated.

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.29.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

